# .vercelignore
#
# The Vercel project's Root Directory build setting points at
# inaya-network-dapp/, but `vercel deploy` run from the monorepo ROOT
# still walks and uploads the FULL working tree regardless of that
# setting -- it doesn't limit what gets bundled, only where the build
# runs once uploaded. Without this file, a deploy pulls in every
# node_modules across every package (inaya-network-dapp/, inaya-mobile/,
# custody-sdk/ and its own sub-packages), .git history, Hardhat build
# artifacts, and prebuilt desktop binaries -- multiple gigabytes of
# content that has nothing to do with what actually gets deployed, which
# is what caused a deploy to hang for 20+ minutes uploading a multi-GB
# archive instead of finishing in under a minute like every other
# deploy of this project.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's exclusions, plus a few more that only matter for
# deploys specifically (this file's own scope is upload-time file
# selection, not what's version-controlled).

node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.next
**/.next

# Separately hosted repos, not part of this deploy's build
inaya-mobile
inaya-network-dapp/custody-sdk

# Hardhat build output -- regenerable, and not needed by the Next.js build
artifacts
cache

# Prebuilt desktop binaries -- large, regenerable, not part of the web deploy
portable-builds

# Local env files -- Vercel's own dashboard-configured env vars are what
# actually apply in production; these should never be uploaded regardless
.env
.env.local
env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local
